{"id":11,"date":"2016-05-16T12:50:26","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:50:26","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/all-england-badminton-2012-semi-finals-hope-for-denmark-despite-the-fall-of-the-big-stars\/"},"modified":"2016-08-31T17:47:31","modified_gmt":"2016-08-31T17:47:31","slug":"all-england-2012-semi-finals-news-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/all-england-2012-semi-finals-news.html","title":{"rendered":"All England Badminton 2012 Semi-Finals: Hope for Denmark Despite the Fall of the Big Stars"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<p>The Danish badminton team found renewed hope at the semi-finals of the Yonex All England Badminton 2012 today.<\/p>\n<p>Their top guns such as <b>Peter Gade, Viktor Axelsen, Tine Baun and Joachim Fischer\/Christinna Pedersen<\/b> were all eliminated in earlier rounds.<\/p>\n<p><b>Thomas Laybourn<\/b> and <b>Kamilla Rytter Juhl<\/b> provided Denmark a glimpse of hope by delivering an outstanding performance to defeat Xu Chen and Ma Jin in 2 straight games (21-16, 21-18).<\/p>\n<p>It has been 7 years since Thomas Laybourn and Kamilla Rytter Juhl competed in the All England final.<\/p>\n<p>They will be playing at the All England finals again after 7 years!<\/p>\n<p>Laybourn and Juhl briefly describe their performance after the match.<\/p>\n<div align=\"center\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/OXt6v775wt4\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\"><\/p>\n<h2>Top 3 Seeds in Mixed Doubles Knocked Out!<\/h2>\n<p>All in all, the top 3 seeds in mixed doubles were eliminated. Apart from the 2nd seeds Xu Chen and Ma Jin getting knocked out, Zhang Nan\/Zhao Yun Lei (CHN)[1] and Joachim Fischer\/Christinna Pedersen (DEN)[3] were out.<\/p>\n<p>The elimination of the top players shows that every player is going all out to produce their best performance. This is mainly due to the attractive BWF ranking points this Premier tournament has to offer.<\/p>\n<p>The lower ranked players are so determined simply because they want to qualify for the upcoming London Olympics 2012.<\/p>\n<p>Players are required to attain the highest BWF ranking points in their respective countries before 3 May 2012, in order to get a rare chance to represent their country in the Olympic Games.<\/p>\n<h3>Lee Chong Wei and Lin Dan Sets up another Meeting in the Final<\/h3>\n<p>2 of the world&#8217;s best and most entertaining singles players will meet at the Yonex All England 2012 final.<\/p>\n<p>Two time defending champion, Lee Chong Wei of Malaysia defeated Lee Hyun Il (KOR) at 21-19, 21-18.<\/p>\n<p>Current World and Olympic champion, Lin Dan defeated Kenichi Tago at 21-18, 21-17.<\/p>\n<p>The 2012 All-England draw has been very kind to the Malaysian. He had not been matched with his nemesis Chen Long or Lin Dan. Lee Chong Wei had a fairly easy path to the All England Finals.<\/p>\n<p>On the other hand, Lin Dan had to face former Olympic champion Taufik Hidayat and Kenichi Tago to get to the final.<\/p>\n<p>Most of you must be thinking that Super Dan would have no problem defeating these players. But he had to put up with a very strong fight to overcome resistance from Taufik and Kenichi. This could have probably tired him out slightly more than Chong Wei&#8217;s opponents.<\/p>\n<h3>Jung Jae Sung and Lee Yong Dae (KOR) too Strong for the Defending Champions<\/h3>\n<p>In men&#8217;s doubles, Mathias Boe\/Carsten Mogensen (DEN) fought with Jung Jae Sung\/Lee Yong Dae for a spot to compete at the All England final.<\/p>\n<p>Frustration was evident as the defending champions Boe and Mogensen realised their attacks were ineffective against the Koreans.<\/p>\n<p>The Danes were forced to exit the tournament after the Koreans defeated them in 2 straight games (21-14, 21-13).<\/p>\n<h3>Chan\/Goh&#8217;s Determination Not Enough<\/h3>\n<p>Based on the earlier performances in the tournament, Chan Peng Soon and Goh Liu Ying of Malaysia looked like they could reach the final of this All England Super Series Premier.<\/p>\n<p>The Malaysian pair was performing very well. Chan Peng Soon controlled the centre and rear court so well. They even defeated the 2011 World Championships silver medallist, Chris Adcock\/Imogen Bankier.<\/p>\n<p>Indonesians Tontowi Ahmad and Liliyana Natsir proved to be too strong. The Malaysians showed great desire to stay in the tournament. The first game dragged on to a 25-point deuce!<\/p>\n<p>In the end, the Malaysians failed to convert their hard work into a victory. The Indonesians proceeded to the final after defeating Chan and Goh at 27-25, 21-16.<\/p>\n<p>However, the Malaysians left the National Indoor Arena with great pride and warm-hearted support from the crowd. It was their first time playing in the semi-finals of the All England.<\/p>\n<p>Malaysia has never been strong in their mixed doubles discipline. Being able to progress so far into a Super Series Premier tournament, Chan and Goh deserved all the support they received.<\/p>\n<div align=\"center\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/MoRd0iJVmPg\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"><\/iframe><\/div>\n<p><\/iframe><\/div>\n<p><a href=\"all-england-badminton-championships-2012-announcement.html\">Go to our announcement page for more details on the competition, how to watch it live, and ticket information<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"yonex-all-england-championships-2012-event-program.html\">event program<\/a> for the match schedules.<\/p>\n<div align=\"center\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Danish badminton team found renewed hope at the semi-finals of the Yonex All England Badminton 2012 today. Their top guns such as Peter Gade, Viktor Axelsen, Tine Baun and Joachim Fischer\/Christinna Pedersen were all eliminated in earlier rounds. Thomas Laybourn and Kamilla Rytter Juhl provided Denmark a glimpse of hope by delivering an outstanding [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[22],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-11","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-badminton-news"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.6 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>All England Badminton 2012 Semi-Finals: Hope for Denmark Despite the Fall of the Big Stars<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"All England badminton 2012 semi finals news\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/all-england-2012-semi-finals-news.html\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"All England Badminton 2012 Semi-Finals: Hope for Denmark Despite the Fall of the Big Stars\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"All England badminton 2012 semi finals news\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/all-england-2012-semi-finals-news.html\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Master Badminton\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2016-05-16T12:50:26+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2016-08-31T17:47:31+00:00\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"3 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"appl